# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# A line longer than the window: the page follows the caret sideways so
# it is never lost off the right edge, and Home brings the whole view
# back.  No wrap -- the line stays one line, and the window slides along
# it.  Proven by the caret: at the line's end it stands near the right
# edge, and Home puts it back at the left with the right edge cleared.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Programming
wait 4
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 150
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
click-window Project
wait 8
key Down
wait 8
key Return
wait 90
expect-title main.bas
note the file opens with the caret at the end of its long last line,
note so the page has already slid to keep the caret near the right edge
key End
wait 6
expect-pixel 790 336 000000
note Home walks the caret to column zero, and the view comes home with
note it: the caret stands at the left, the right edge cleared
key Home
wait 6
expect-pixel 196 336 000000
expect-pixel 790 336 ffffff
quit
